Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.350 align:start position:0%
 
i take food  so seriously because it literally saved  my life  i needed a reason to get out of bed  every day i needed a reason to  continue to live and be and exist on  this earth and that was baking  my name is brianna jackson i'm a  professional pastry chef from  los angeles california and i'm the proud  owner and head baker  for sugar and spice baked by brie  i even started the business honestly i  was always in the kitchen with my  grandmother growing up  of course for holiday meals cooking  things with her but  when i got older and would just get  frustrated or have like a really bad day  the first thing i do is put things down  in the house and go straight to the  kitchen  and just look around in the pantry in  the fridge and say  what can i create that'll bring me joy  right now or what can i do that would  just make me happy and  it was always in the kitchen once i got  into the kitchen mostly stuck  to sweets and that's kind of what i was  most comfortable with i was  experimenting with cakes  with cupcakes especially different types  of cookies if i'm going to a friend's  party or a birthday party  i baked it was okay if you go mama  always told  you never go anywhere empty-handed so  get in that kitchen  make something and every time i went to  a function and had a dessert with me  everyone loved it and they text me oh my  god girl you did your thing in this  like wow this is amazing this is the  best dressed leches i've ever had like  just have someone tell you that it feels  amazing  there's something about food that just  it makes you happy  when you bite into it it just warms your  soul  and if i can provide that for someone  else that just fills me with joy  i knew in middle school i wanted to go  to culinary school  i unfortunately just didn't have the  privilege or the accessibility to really  pursue that it was always you know  get a traditional education first and  maybe if you're still passionate about  it then  at least you have a fallback the entire  four years i was in college all my  friends found me  in the kitchen brianna's making cookies  or briana's making cupcakes or brianna's  doing something in that kitchen everyone  just knew  food has just always been there it's  always been something i've wanted and  wanted to pursue  forever  i started sugar and spice in september  of 2016.  it's been almost four years now starting  a business  when i did especially in that time was  not at all planned  when i would do events and pop-ups and  things of that nature people would  always ask me oh my gosh like what made  you start your business how did you get  here and  i would lie and say it felt like the  right time it felt like the right thing  to do  in truth it was born out of one of the  most dramatic things that's happened to  me  sugar and spice started four years ago  and four years ago i was relearning how  to  live exist and even be any longer  it was august 4th 2016.  i was raped by someone i know  and that moment absolutely broke me  it surpassed any pain i've ever dealt  with in my life  the emotional pain the mental pain the  physical pain  it was to the point where i questioned  life i questioned  spirituality and religion and everything  and everyone like  why why me because of that  and how i dealt with it and internalized  it  and tried to move forward from it it  kind of sparked the business  i needed a purpose i needed a reason to  get out of bed every day  i needed a reason to continue to live  and be and exist on this earth and that  was baking  it's weird because i would go days  without eating  but i was still somehow cooking for  others  i was caring for my grandmother and i  may be sad  and hurt in so many ways but  my grandma's like the love of my life so  that's never going to stop me from  cooking for her  and bringing her some happiness because  in turn  it makes me a little happier i'm feeling  at my absolute lowest and my absolute  worst  but yet i'm still able to produce  something that brings others happiness  all right maybe there's something there  maybe this can  really help me and bring me a little  more joy back into my life  food has always represented security  it's been  joyful and provided a happy place for me  that was something at that point in my  life  i was really lacking and searching for  and trying to find again  i found the sanctuary and sanctioned in  the  in the kitchen before i found it in  anyone else and even myself  the kitchen was just i knew that was  always the place for me when i was  younger  so i said you know what maybe it can  help now  i have been through so much loss in my  life  and then with the rape i lost myself so  to have all these losses it's just like  i gotta find myself i need to have a win  and that win was  sugar and spice baked by bree  as traumatizing as that moment was it  was  the life change that pushed me to pursue  my passions  full-fledged full force no longer  holding back say you know i've wanted  this my entire life life is too short  to not pursue your dreams there's  nothing holding me back  and i'm going for it since then  i've developed recipes and had a dish  on a menu at a restaurant i worked at i  have been  a kitchen manager i have been  front of the house back of the house as  far as  any job within the food industry you  name it i've done it at this point  i don't think i started to feel like  myself again until i finally just  jumped into pursuing food full time my  favorite tattoo that i have  is my chef's tattoo and it's my favorite  quote from  nipt hustle find your purpose or you're  wasting air and this is my  very first chef's knife that i got my  purpose is to cook to be in somebody's  kitchen somewhere in the world  and just produce food that i love that  i'm proud of and proud to say hey i  created this  when someone's eating one of my  creations i'm just i'm profoundly just  happy  that is when i finally felt like me  i really started this journey selfishly  and this business was like a selfish  thing  for me this business helped me find  myself again  and since i've been open about it and  opening up to more people about it  now this business it's not even about me  i really hope  i can help someone else through this  journey like yeah i want you to be happy  when you taste my food but like  there's so much more to it like there's  so much more to food than people think  it is  food is life-changing  if i could talk to me four years ago  oh baby girl you are  so much stronger than you think um  you have so far to go and you are as  great as people have been telling you  your entire life  this this is the moment but it only gets  better from here  like keep please keep fighting  i think i could summarize my story in  one word and that is survival  no matter how difficult the roads have  been  how many events i've done where i might  not even sell a single thing  i'm still gonna survive i'm gonna find a  way to take that  learn from it grow from it and continue  to move forward  i love food food definitely helps me  love myself  a little harder i will never give it up  food  absolutely saved my life  my name is brianna breezy jackson proud  owner of sugar and spice baked by breed  and i'm following my food dreams  you

